0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Intel 8080
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-23).
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm), with 8080 opcodes
0000                             ;  only.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ;    ANSI     1 = the four console codes (`@ `^ `_ `?) send ANSI escape
0000                             ;                 sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = they call four routines of the machine's own instead:
0000                             ;                 CONAT, CONCLS, CONEOL and CONCUR (see the equates)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), I8080 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console codes send ANSI sequences
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the 8080"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The return stack pointer has no register (the 8080 has no spare pair): it
0000                             ;  is the RAM word RSP. Only rpop, rpushd and ")" (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three. (asm80 wants the vector number: RST 1 = RST 08h.)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 1  08h  rpop    pop the return stack into HL
0000                             ;    RST 3  18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 4  20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 5  28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 6  30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 3 and RST 6 never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing each
0000                             ;  of them does is POP D to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block has no jumps inside itself, so it works at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  What the 8080 lacks, and what replaces it: no JR (JMP/Jcc), no DJNZ, no
0000                             ;  SBC HL (byte-wise SUB/SBB, or negate and DAD), no shifts on register pairs
0000                             ;  (DAD H doubles; RAL/RAR through A), no LDIR/CPIR (small loops).
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with ORA A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE and HL.
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-ANSI)   
                                 ; ---- generic machine with ANSI = 0: the console codes call these ------------
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF0Ch   ; `@  cursor to row E, column L, both from 0
                                 ;     (DE and HL hold the whole cells). May
                                 ;     change A, DE and HL
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; `^  clear the screen and home the cursor
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF12h   ; `_  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF15h   ; `?  cursor off if A = 0 (the zero flag is set
                                 ;     to match), on if not. May change A, DE, HL
                                 ;   All four must preserve BC; CONCLS and CONEOL also DE and HL.
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255;
0000                             ; the wait for a second Ctrl-C uses it too):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSP:      EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: the return stack pointer;
0000                BRKCNT:   EQU   LET+36h   ;   the break check's countdown;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_'
0000                SEED:     EQU   LET+76h   ; gap after z: the random seed, the cell whose
0000                             ;   address `. gives. Nothing sets it at the
0000                             ;   start but the checked build's clearing;
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ;   a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   1-(1-CPM)*CHECKED   
0100   31 FC 09               LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103   C3 E4 06               JMP   start   ; In the checked generic build this is at 0000h
0106                             ;   (and `start` sets SP): its first byte, C3h,
0106                             ;   is what an undefined word runs into, as
0106                             ;   CP/M's own JMP at 0000h is in a .COM: e_hi.
0106                          IF   (1-CPM)*CHECKED   
                              DB   0,0,0   ; 03  spare
0106                          ENDIF      
0106   CF           RDROP:    RST   1   ; 06  drop the top of the return stack, then
0107   DF                     RST   3   ;     drop TOS (a spent flag) and go on
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 1: rpop: pop the return stack into HL (DE is lost) -----------------
0108   2A 34 0A     RPOP:     LHLD   RSP   ; 08
010B   5E                     MOV   E,M   
010C   23                     INX   H   
010D   56                     MOV   D,M   
010E   23                     INX   H   
010F   22 34 0A               SHLD   RSP   
0112   EB                     XCHG      
0113   C9                     RET      ; 13  (so RST 2 is not used)
0114   EB           H_TOR:    XCHG      ; 14  "{" TOS to the return stack; rpushd
0115   C3 B7 01               JMP   rpushd   ;     brings up the new TOS
0118                             ; ---- RST 3: drop TOS, then next ---------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   D   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   H   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   C3 34 01               JMP   next0   
011D   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   H   ; 1D  "}" return stack to TOS
011E   CF                     RST   1   
011F   F7                     RST   6   
0120                             ; ---- RST 4: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) ----------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XRA   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBB   A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     MOV   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   E9           JPHL:     PCHL      ; 27  (for the machine-code call)
0128                             ; ---- RST 5: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL) --------------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 47 05               JMP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B                             ; exec: "`" with no hex digit after it: call the machine code at TOS. It
012B                             ; returns here, with its top cell on the stack: that becomes the new TOS.
012B   CD 27 01     EXEC:     CALL   jphl   ; 2B
012E   E1                     POP   H   
012F   F7                     RST   6   
0130                             ; ---- RST 6: next character --------------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   D   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JMP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
0134   CD B5 05               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0137                          ENDIF      
0137   0A                     LDAX   B   
0138   03                     INX   B   
0139   D6 21                  SUI   21h   ; A = c - 21h
013B   DA 7E 01               JC   ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013E   FE 0F                  CPI   0Fh   
0140   DA 6E 01               JC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0143   D6 0F                  SUI   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0145   FE 0A                  CPI   0Ah   
0147   DA 4B 03               JC   digit   ; 30h-39h
014A   FE 11                  CPI   11h   
014C   DA 6C 01               JC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
014F   D6 11                  SUI   11h   ; A = c - 41h
0151   FE 1A                  CPI   1Ah   
0153   DA AD 01               JC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0156   FE 20                  CPI   20h   
0158   DA 6A 01               JC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
015B   FE 3A                  CPI   3Ah   
015D   DA A7 01               JC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0160   FE 3E                  CPI   3Eh   
0162                          IF   CHECKED   
0162   CA 34 01               JZ   next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
0165   D2 EC 05               JNC   e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
0168                          ENDIF      
0168                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JNC   next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0168                          ENDIF      
0168   D6 1A                  SUI   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
016A   D6 09        P5B:      SUI   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
016C   C6 05        P3A:      ADI   5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
016E                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
016E                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
016E   C6 2B        PUNCT:    ADI   PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0170   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0171   16 03                  MVI   D,PTAB / 256   
0173   FE 41                  CPI   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0175   1A                     LDAX   D   
0176   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0177                          IFN   CPM   
                              MVI   A,0   
                              RAL      ; its page: 0 + carry
0177                          ENDIF      
0177                          IF   CPM   
0177   3E 01                  MVI   A,1   
0179   CE 00                  ACI   0   ; its page: 1 + carry
017B                          ENDIF      
017B   57                     MOV   D,A   
017C   D5                     PUSH   D   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
017D   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
017E                             ; ctl: characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
017E   C6 21        CTL:      ADI   21h   ; back to c; zero only for NUL
0180   C2 34 01               JNZ   next0   ; the rest are ignored
0183   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
0186                             ; =============================================================================
0186                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0186                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.)
0186                             ; =============================================================================
0186   D1           H_XOR:    POP   D   
0187   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0188   AA                     XRA   D   
0189   67                     MOV   H,A   
018A   7D                     MOV   A,L   
018B   AB                     XRA   E   
018C   6F                     MOV   L,A   
018D   F7                     RST   6   
018E   D1           H_OR:     POP   D   
018F   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0190   B2                     ORA   D   
0191   67                     MOV   H,A   
0192   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0193   B3                     ORA   E   
0194   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0195   F7                     RST   6   
0196   E7           H_NOT:    RST   4   ; ~x = -x - 1
0197   2B                     DCX   H   
0198   F7                     RST   6   
0199                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0199                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0199   EB           H_ALLOC:   XCHG      
019A   2A 7C 0A               LHLD   HEAP   
019D   E5                     PUSH   H   
019E   19                     DAD   D   ; the new top
019F                          IF   CHECKED   
019F   CD 55 05               CALL   chkhp   
01A2                          ENDIF      
01A2   22 7C 0A               SHLD   HEAP   
01A5   E1                     POP   H   
01A6   F7                     RST   6   
01A7                             ; ---- the letters and digits --------------------------------------------------
01A7                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01A7   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   H   
01A8   87                     ADD   A   
01A9   6F                     MOV   L,A   
01AA   26 0A                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   
01AC   F7                     RST   6   
01AD                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01AD                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01AD   E5           UPPER:    PUSH   H   ; keep TOS: rpushd pops it back
01AE   87                     ADD   A   
01AF   6F                     MOV   L,A   
01B0   26 0A                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01B2   50                     MOV   D,B   
01B3   59                     MOV   E,C   ; DE = the return address
01B4   4E                     MOV   C,M   
01B5   23                     INX   H   
01B6   46                     MOV   B,M   ; IP = the word's body, and fall into rpushd
01B7                             ; rpushd: push DE on the return stack, then pop TOS off the data stack and
01B7                             ; go on. Every push of the return stack ends here: for a word call the cell
01B7                             ; popped is the TOS that upper parked; for "(" and "{" it is the cell under
01B7                             ; the one that was used up.
01B7                             ; 
01B7                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
01B7                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: BRKCNT counts them. Reading
01B7                             ; the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call under CP/M).
01B7   2A 34 0A     RPUSHD:   LHLD   RSP   
01BA   2B                     DCX   H   
01BB   72                     MOV   M,D   
01BC   2B                     DCX   H   
01BD   73                     MOV   M,E   
01BE   22 34 0A               SHLD   RSP   
01C1   21 36 0A               LXI   H,BRKCNT   
01C4   35                     DCR   M   
01C5   E1                     POP   H   ; (keeps the flags)
01C6   CC 02 05               CZ   pollk   
01C9   F7                     RST   6   
01CA                             ; ---- the grave -------------------------------------------------------------
01CA                             ; The grave is a prefix: with the character after it, it is one command.
01CA                             ; GTAB holds each character with the place of its handler, as a byte to add
01CA                             ; to gbase. The handler starts with HL = TOS, A = the character and the
01CA                             ; carry clear. A character that is not in the table is unsafe: the unchecked
01CA                             ; build searches on through memory, the checked build stops with W.
01CA   0A           H_GRAVE:   LDAX   B   
01CB   03                     INX   B   
01CC   E5                     PUSH   H   ; TOS
01CD   21 61 04               LXI   H,GTAB-1   
01D0   23           GR1:      INX   H   
01D1                          IF   CHECKED   
01D1   5E                     MOV   E,M   
01D2   1C                     INR   E   
01D3   CA 5E 04               JZ   gbad   ; FFh ends the table
01D6                          ENDIF      
01D6   BE                     CMP   M   
01D7   23                     INX   H   
01D8   C2 D0 01               JNZ   gr1   
01DB   5E                     MOV   E,M   
01DC   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
01DE   21 A0 03               LXI   H,gbase   
01E1   19                     DAD   D   ; the handler
01E2   E3                     XTHL      ; TOS back, and jump there
01E3   C9                     RET      
01E4                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01E4                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01E4                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01E4                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01E4                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01E4                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. TOS is parked on the stack
01E4                             ; while rpop uses HL, and the drop at the end brings it back.
01E4   E5           H_RET:    PUSH   H   
01E5   CF           RET2:     RST   1   
01E6   44                     MOV   B,H   
01E7   4D                     MOV   C,L   
01E8   DF                     RST   3   
01E9                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01E9                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01E9                             ; The flag stays in HL as the spent cell that rdrop and ret2 drop.
01E9   7C           H_BREAK:   MOV   A,H   
01EA   B5                     ORA   L   
01EB   CA D6 02               JZ   h_drop   ; false: just drop the flag
01EE   CD 98 04               CALL   skip   
01F1   B7                     ORA   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01F2   C2 E5 01               JNZ   ret2   
01F5   C3 06 01               JMP   rdrop   
01F8                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01F8                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01F8                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01F8                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01F8                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01F8   0A           H_DEF:    LDAX   B   
01F9   03                     INX   B   
01FA   D6 41                  SUI   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
01FC   5F                     MOV   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
01FD   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   ; fold case
01FF   FE 1A                  CPI   26   
0201   D2 11 02               JNC   def2   ; not a letter
0204   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0205   87                     ADD   A   
0206   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0207   16 0A                  MVI   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
0209   79                     MOV   A,C   
020A   12                     STAX   D   
020B   1C                     INR   E   
020C   78                     MOV   A,B   
020D   12                     STAX   D   
020E   C3 1A 02               JMP   skipnx   
0211                DEF2:        
0211                          IF   CHECKED   
0211   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0212   FE DF                  CPI   " "-"A"+256   
0214   C2 06 06               JNZ   e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0217                          ENDIF      
0217   E5                     PUSH   H   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0218   60                     MOV   H,B   
0219   69                     MOV   L,C   
021A                SKIPNX:      
021A                          IF   CHECKED   
021A   0B                     DCX   B   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
021B                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
021B   CD 98 04     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
021E   F7                     RST   6   
021F   5E           H_FETCH:   MOV   E,M   ; "@"
0220   23                     INX   H   
0221   56                     MOV   D,M   
0222   EB                     XCHG      
0223   F7                     RST   6   
0224                             ; =============================================================================
0224                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0224                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it in the unchecked build), so its long
0224                             ;  tail may run past that page.
0224                             ; =============================================================================
0224                             ; ---- flow control ----------------------------------------------------------
0224                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0224                             ; the matching ")".
0224   7C           H_OPEN:   MOV   A,H   
0225   B5                     ORA   L   
0226   E1                     POP   H   
0227   CA 1B 02               JZ   skipo   
022A   E5                     PUSH   H   ; (rpushd pops it again)
022B   50                     MOV   D,B   
022C   59                     MOV   E,C   ; the block starts at the IP
022D   C3 B7 01               JMP   rpushd   
0230                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
0230                             ; drops it and carries on.
0230   7C           H_CLOSE:   MOV   A,H   
0231   B5                     ORA   L   
0232   CA 06 01               JZ   rdrop   
0235   CF                     RST   1   ; pop the block start ...
0236   44                     MOV   B,H   
0237   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; ... jump to it ...
0238   EB                     XCHG      
0239   C3 B7 01               JMP   rpushd   ; ... and push it back (which drops the flag)
023C                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
023C                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
023C   0A           H_SUB:    LDAX   B   
023D   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
023F   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0241   DA 51 03               JC   negnum   
0244   E7                     RST   4   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0245   D1           H_ADD:    POP   D   
0246   19                     DAD   D   
0247   F7                     RST   6   
0248   D1           H_AND:    POP   D   
0249   7C                     MOV   A,H   
024A   A2                     ANA   D   
024B   67                     MOV   H,A   
024C   7D                     MOV   A,L   
024D   A3                     ANA   E   
024E   6F                     MOV   L,A   
024F   F7                     RST   6   
0250                             ; Signed compares. Both are "DE < HL" for the right pair: > swaps the two
0250                             ; cells first (XTHL), < doesn't. There is no overflow flag, so the signed
0250                             ; answer is the unsigned borrow of DE - HL, flipped when the signs differ.
0250                             ; SBB A turns a carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
0250   E3           H_GT:     XTHL      ; a > b  is  b < a
0251   D1           H_LT:     POP   D   ; a < b: DE = a, HL = b
0252   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0253   95                     SUB   L   
0254   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0255   9C                     SBB   H   
0256   9F                     SBB   A   ; A = -1 if DE < HL unsigned
0257   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0258   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0259   AA                     XRA   D   
025A   17                     RAL      ; carry = the signs differ
025B   9F                     SBB   A   
025C   AD                     XRA   L   ; flip when they do
025D   67                     MOV   H,A   
025E   6F                     MOV   L,A   
025F   F7                     RST   6   
0260   D1           H_EQ:     POP   D   
0261   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0262   AB                     XRA   E   
0263   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0264   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0265   AA                     XRA   D   
0266   B5                     ORA   L   ; zero if equal
0267   D6 01                  SUI   1   ; carry only for zero
0269   9F                     SBB   A   
026A   67                     MOV   H,A   
026B   6F                     MOV   L,A   
026C   F7                     RST   6   
026D                             ; "*": shift-and-add on the multiplier's low bit, so it stops as soon as the
026D                             ; multiplier is used up; only the low 16 bits are kept.
026D   D1           H_MUL:    POP   D   ; DE = multiplicand
026E   C5                     PUSH   B   
026F   44                     MOV   B,H   
0270   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; BC = multiplier
0271   21 00 00               LXI   H,0   
0274   78           MUL1:     MOV   A,B   
0275   B7                     ORA   A   ; clear carry
0276   1F                     RAR      
0277   47                     MOV   B,A   
0278   79                     MOV   A,C   
0279   1F                     RAR      
027A   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; BC >> 1, carry = the bit shifted out
027B   D2 7F 02               JNC   mul2   
027E   19                     DAD   D   
027F   EB           MUL2:     XCHG      
0280   29                     DAD   H   ; multiplicand << 1
0281   EB                     XCHG      
0282   78                     MOV   A,B   
0283   B1                     ORA   C   
0284   C2 74 02               JNZ   mul1   
0287   C1                     POP   B   
0288   F7                     RST   6   
0289                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
0289                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
0289                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
0289                             ; stops on it.
0289                H_DIV:       
0289                          IF   CHECKED   
0289   7C                     MOV   A,H   
028A   B5                     ORA   L   
028B   CA 03 06               JZ   e_zero   
028E                          ENDIF      
028E   D1                     POP   D   ; DE = a, HL = b
028F   C5                     PUSH   B   
0290   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0291   B7                     ORA   A   
0292   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of a (for r)
0293   AC                     XRA   H   
0294   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of q
0295   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0296   B7                     ORA   A   
0297   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; HL = |b|
029A   EB                     XCHG      
029B   7C                     MOV   A,H   
029C   B7                     ORA   A   
029D   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
02A0   CD 6E 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, BC = r
02A3   F1                     POP   PSW   
02A4   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; q's sign
02A7   EB                     XCHG      ; DE = q
02A8   60                     MOV   H,B   
02A9   69                     MOV   L,C   ; HL = r
02AA   F1                     POP   PSW   
02AB   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; r's sign
02AE   C1                     POP   B   
02AF   D5                     PUSH   D   ; q under r
02B0   F7                     RST   6   
02B1                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
02B1   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   H   ; ":"
02B2   F7                     RST   6   
02B3   E3           H_SWAP:   XTHL      ; "%"
02B4   F7                     RST   6   
02B5                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
02B5                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
02B5                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
02B5                          IF   CHECKED   
02B5   CD 75 05               CALL   chkst   
02B8                          ENDIF      
02B8   D1                     POP   D   
02B9   73                     MOV   M,E   
02BA   23                     INX   H   
02BB   72                     MOV   M,D   
02BC   DF                     RST   3   
02BD                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
02BD                          IF   CHECKED   
02BD   CD 75 05               CALL   chkst   
02C0                          ENDIF      
02C0   D1                     POP   D   
02C1   73                     MOV   M,E   
02C2   DF                     RST   3   
02C3                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
02C3                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
02C3   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   H   
02C4   60                     MOV   H,B   
02C5   69                     MOV   L,C   
02C6   CD DC 04               CALL   skipstr   
02C9                          IF   CHECKED   
02C9   B7                     ORA   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
02CA   CA FB 05               JZ   e_quote   
02CD                          ENDIF      
02CD   F7                     RST   6   
02CE                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
02CE                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
02CE                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
02CE                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JZ   h_drop   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JNZ   pr1   
                              MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              ANI   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   5   
                              JMP   h_print   
02CE                          ENDIF      
02CE                          IF   CHECKED   
02CE                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
02CE                             ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
02CE                             ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
02CE   E5           H_PRINT:   PUSH   H   
02CF   CD 8C 05               CALL   prstr   
02D2   D1                     POP   D   
02D3   DF                     RST   3   
02D4                          ENDIF      
02D4   7D           H_EMIT:   MOV   A,L   ; "'"
02D5   EF                     RST   5   
02D6   DF           H_DROP:   RST   3   ; ";" is this one byte
02D7                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02D7   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   B   
02D8   CD 7D 04               CALL   psgn   
02DB   C1                     POP   B   
02DC   DF                     RST   3   
02DD                          IF   CHECKED   ; (the checked build has no room to start ","
02DD   6E           H_CFETCH:   MOV   L,M   ;   as late as the unchecked one does: see
02DE   26 00                  MVI   H,0   ;   the end of "?")
02E0   F7                     RST   6   
02E1                          ENDIF      
02E1                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02E1                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02E1                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02E1                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02E1                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02E1   7C           H_KEY:    MOV   A,H   
02E2   B7                     ORA   A   
02E3   FA 0A 03               JM   line   
02E6   1E 28        KT1:      MVI   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02E8   CD 34 05     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02EB   C2 06 03               JNZ   kt3   
02EE   1D                     DCR   E   
02EF   C2 E8 02               JNZ   kt2   
02F2   EB                     XCHG      ; a millisecond with no key stirs the random
02F3   2A 76 0A               LHLD   SEED   ;   seed by one: how long a key takes to come
02F6   23                     INX   H   ;   is the one thing here that is not the
02F7   22 76 0A               SHLD   SEED   ;   same every time
02FA   EB                     XCHG      
02FB   7C                     MOV   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
02FC   B5                     ORA   L   
02FD   CA E6 02               JZ   kt1   
0300   2B                     DCX   H   
0301   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0302   B5                     ORA   L   
0303   C2 E6 02               JNZ   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
0306                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              DB   0FEh   ; (CPI: steps over the one byte of ",")
                    H_CFETCH:   MOV   A,M   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
0306                          ENDIF      
0306   6F           KT3:      MOV   L,A   
0307   26 00                  MVI   H,0   
0309   F7                     RST   6   
030A                          IF   CPM   
030A                             ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
030A                             ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
030A   11 7F 00     LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
030D   19                     DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
030E   9F                     SBB   A   
030F   A5                     ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
0310   EE 7F                  XRI   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
0312   32 7E 0A               STA   LBHDR   
0315   C5                     PUSH   B   
0316   11 7E 0A               LXI   D,LBHDR   
0319   0E 0A                  MVI   C,10   
031B   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
031E   C1                     POP   B   
031F   21 7F 0A               LXI   H,LBHDR+1   
0322   7E                     MOV   A,M   ; the count typed (0-127)
0323   2C                     INR   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
0324   85                     ADD   L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
0325   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0326   36 0D                  MVI   M,13   
0328   2E 80                  MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
032A   F7                     RST   6   
032B                          ENDIF      
032B                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
                                 ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
                                 ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
                                 ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
                                 ; a full line.
                    LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBB   A   
                              ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              CMA      
                              MOV   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
                                 ;   at most
                              LXI   H,LINEBUF   
                    LN2:      CALL   getk   
                              JZ   ln2   
                              CPI   13   
                              JZ   ln5   
                              CPI   8   
                              JZ   ln4   
                              MOV   E,A   
                              MOV   A,L   
                              CMP   D   
                              JZ   ln2   ; full
                              MOV   M,E   
                              INR   L   
                              MOV   A,E   
                    LN3:      RST   5   
                              JMP   ln2   
                    LN4:      DCR   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
                              JM   ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
                              INR   L   ;   upper half of the page)
                              JMP   ln2   
                    LN5:      MOV   M,A   ; the CR
                              MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
                              RST   6   
032B                          ENDIF      
032B                             ; =============================================================================
032B                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order.
032B                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
032B                             ; =============================================================================
032B                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
032B                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
032B                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
032B                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
032B                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
032B                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
032B                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
032B                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
032B                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
032B   B5           PTAB:     DB   h_store & 0FFh   ; !
032C   C3                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   ; "
032D   D7                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   ; #
032E   CE                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   ; $
032F   B3                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0330   48                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   ; &
0331   D4                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0332   24                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0333   30                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   ; )
0334   6D                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   ; *
0335   45                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   ; +
0336   DD                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   ; ,
0337   3C                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   ; -
0338   BD                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   ; .
0339   89                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   ; /
033A   B1                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   ; :
033B   D6                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
033C   51                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   ; <
033D   60                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   ; =
033E   50                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   ; >
033F   E1                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   ; ?
0340   1F                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   ; @
0341   F8                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   ; [
0342   E9                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   ; \
0343   E4                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   ; ]
0344   86                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   ; ^
0345   99                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   ; _
0346   CA                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   ; `
0347   14                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   ; {
0348   8E                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   ; |
0349   1D                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   ; }
034A   96                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   ; ~
034B                PTABEND:      
034B                             ; =============================================================================
034B                             ;  Routines (no handler starts past this point)
034B                             ; =============================================================================
034B                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
034B   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   H   
034C   0B                     DCX   B   
034D   CD 57 03               CALL   rdnum   
0350   F7                     RST   6   
0351                             ; negnum: "-" directly before a digit: read the number, negate it.
0351   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   H   
0352   CD 57 03               CALL   rdnum   
0355   E7                     RST   4   
0356   F7                     RST   6   
0357                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
0357                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
0357   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LXI   H,0   
035A   0A           RDN1:     LDAX   B   
035B   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
035D   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
035F   D0                     RNC      
0360   03                     INX   B   
0361   54                     MOV   D,H   
0362   5D                     MOV   E,L   
0363   29                     DAD   H   
0364   29                     DAD   H   
0365   19                     DAD   D   
0366   29                     DAD   H   ; HL * 10
0367   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0368   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
036A   19                     DAD   D   
036B   C3 5A 03               JMP   rdn1   
036E                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, BC = remainder.
036E                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. HL holds the dividend and, as its bits
036E                             ; leave at the top, the quotient bits arrive at the bottom. The loop counter
036E                             ; lives on the stack, since A is busy with the shifts.
036E                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
036E   01 00 00     UDIV:     LXI   B,0   
0371   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0372   EE 02                  XRI   2   
0374   B2                     ORA   D   
0375   C2 82 03               JNZ   udv0   
0378   B4                     ORA   H   ; A was 0, and the carry is clear
0379   1F                     RAR      
037A   67                     MOV   H,A   
037B   7D                     MOV   A,L   
037C   1F                     RAR      
037D   6F                     MOV   L,A   ; the quotient
037E   78                     MOV   A,B   
037F   17                     RAL      
0380   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
0381   C9                     RET      
0382   3E 10        UDV0:     MVI   A,16   
0384   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
0385   29           UDV1:     DAD   H   ; next dividend bit into the carry
0386   79                     MOV   A,C   
0387   17                     RAL      
0388   4F                     MOV   C,A   
0389   78                     MOV   A,B   
038A   17                     RAL      
038B   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC = BC*2 + bit
038C   79                     MOV   A,C   
038D   93                     SUB   E   
038E   78                     MOV   A,B   
038F   9A                     SBB   D   ; carry if BC < DE
0390   DA 98 03               JC   udv2   
0393   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC - DE (high byte; A holds it)
0394   79                     MOV   A,C   
0395   93                     SUB   E   
0396   4F                     MOV   C,A   
0397   2C                     INR   L   ; quotient bit
0398   F1           UDV2:     POP   PSW   
0399   3D                     DCR   A   
039A   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
039B   C2 85 03               JNZ   udv1   
039E   F1                     POP   PSW   
039F   C9                     RET      
03A0                             ; =============================================================================
03A0                             ;  The grave's codes (h_grave is the dispatcher). Each starts with HL = TOS,
03A0                             ;  A = the character and the carry clear.
03A0                             ; 
03A0                             ;    `!  ( addr -- )        call the machine code at addr (exec)
03A0                             ;    `$  ( addr -- addr' )  the hex loader
03A0                             ;    `'  ( -- )             new line: CR LF
03A0                             ;    `+  ( addr -- n )      add 1 to the cell at addr and leave its new value
03A0                             ;    `,  ( n -- r )         a random number from 0 to n-1 (n is 1 to 32767)
03A0                             ;    `-  ( addr -- n )      subtract 1 from the cell at addr, the same way
03A0                             ;    `.  ( -- addr )        the address of the random seed
03A0                             ;    `<  ( a b -- n )       the smaller of the two (signed)
03A0                             ;    `>  ( a b -- n )       the larger
03A0                             ;    `?  ( flag -- )        the cursor off (0) or on
03A0                             ;    `@  ( row col -- )     the cursor to that row and column, both from 0
03A0                             ;    `^  ( -- )             clear the screen and home the cursor
03A0                             ;    `_  ( -- )             clear from the cursor to the end of the line
03A0                             ; =============================================================================
03A0                GBASE:       
03A0   C3 2B 01     G_EXEC:   JMP   exec   ; (exec is up among the RST routines)
03A3                             ; `$: pairs of hex digits are stored from addr until a non-hex character;
03A3                             ; then a RET (C9h) is written and its address is left. An odd last digit is
03A3                             ; consumed and dropped.
03A3   CD EF 04     G_HEX:    CALL   hexc   
03A6   D2 BA 03               JNC   hx2   
03A9   87                     ADD   A   
03AA   87                     ADD   A   
03AB   87                     ADD   A   
03AC   87                     ADD   A   
03AD   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the high digit
03AE   CD EF 04               CALL   hexc   
03B1   D2 BA 03               JNC   hx2   ; odd digit: consumed and dropped
03B4   B2                     ORA   D   
03B5   77                     MOV   M,A   
03B6   23                     INX   H   
03B7   C3 A3 03               JMP   g_hex   
03BA   36 C9        HX2:      MVI   M,0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
03BC   F7                     RST   6   
03BD   3E 0D        G_NL:     MVI   A,13   
03BF   EF                     RST   5   
03C0   3E 0A                  MVI   A,10   
03C2   EF                     RST   5   
03C3   F7                     RST   6   
03C4                             ; `+ and `-: one routine. The character says which.
03C4                G_INC:       
03C4                          IF   CHECKED   
03C4   CD 75 05               CALL   chkst   ; the address is tested first, as "!" does
03C7   0B                     DCX   B   
03C8   0A                     LDAX   B   ; (the test used A: the character again)
03C9   03                     INX   B   
03CA                          ENDIF      
03CA   FE 2C                  CPI   ","   ; carry for "+"
03CC   5E                     MOV   E,M   
03CD   23                     INX   H   
03CE   56                     MOV   D,M   
03CF   D2 D4 03               JNC   gi1   
03D2   13                     INX   D   
03D3   13                     INX   D   
03D4   1B           GI1:      DCX   D   
03D5   72                     MOV   M,D   
03D6   2B                     DCX   H   
03D7   73                     MOV   M,E   
03D8   EB                     XCHG      ; the new value is TOS
03D9   F7                     RST   6   
03DA                             ; `. pushes the address of the random seed.
03DA   E5           G_SEED:   PUSH   H   
03DB   21 76 0A               LXI   H,SEED   
