03DF                             ; `, ( n -- r ). The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes
03DF                             ; every 16-bit value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones
03DF                             ; and the low ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low
03DF                             ; (XOR) before the remainder of dividing by n is taken.
03DF                             ; n must be 1 to 32767: the checked build stops with Z on anything less
03DF                             ; than 1.
03DF                G_RND:       
