0401                             ; round if the two signs differ: RAR puts the borrow in bit 7, where the two
0401                             ; XRAs meet it. Then the character is read again, 3Ch or 3Eh: RAR leaves
0401                             ; 1Eh or 1Fh under the flag, and adding 61h carries into the flag for 1Fh
0401                             ; only. So the carry ends up saying "keep b" for either character.
