05B5                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
05B5                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
05B5                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
05B5                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
05B5                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
05B5                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile.
05B5   EB           CHKSTK:   XCHG      ; DE = TOS (HL is needed for the pointers)
